00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.100
Where shall we go? That sounds wonderful.

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:22.020
The new algorithms have completely taken over his program.

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:22.700
Ambassador!

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.120
So now he's daydreaming constantly?

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.710
It's a photonic cannon. I designed it myself.

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:29.830
He seems to be randomly jumping from one to the next.

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:31.900
Pardon me, miss?

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:33.860
I routed his subroutines to holodeck one

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:36.000
so Harry and Seven could monitor his fantasies.

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.440
You think that's appropriate?

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.440
They're his fantasies.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.250
And I promised him you'd show a little more consideration.

00:23:42.570 --> 00:23:44.450
It'll give us a better idea of what's going on.

00:23:44.530 --> 00:23:45.310
Help us fix him.

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:47.290
Mr. Neelix, how thoughtful.

00:23:48.330 --> 00:23:49.170
You baked me a cake.

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:51.010
Kim to sick bay.

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:52.290
Go ahead, Harry.

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:54.570
You might want to have a look at this.

00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:56.280
We're on our way.

00:24:10.130 --> 00:24:29.850
keep still please anything you say doctor he does the hands apparently he's had a great deal of

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.750
Look at these.

00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:50.160
Computer, activate the emergency command hologram.

00:24:50.660 --> 00:24:52.680
Art I like.

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:57.720
Match.

00:24:58.300 --> 00:24:59.860
Bring the photonic cannon online.

00:25:00.780 --> 00:25:01.640
Clotonic cannon?

00:25:02.350 --> 00:25:05.250
Weapon of mass destruction, invented by the Doctor, of course.

00:25:05.540 --> 00:25:05.980
Of course.

00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:09.320
In many of his fantasies, he takes command and saves the ship.

00:25:09.790 --> 00:25:10.230
I see.

00:25:10.870 --> 00:25:14.070
Which means that particular algorithm is more easily accessible than the others.

00:25:14.460 --> 00:25:17.800
So, if we can isolate it, we might be able to stabilize his program.

00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:19.600
Why do you torment me like this?

00:25:19.860 --> 00:25:21.280
That was never my intention.

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:22.570
It wasn't.

00:25:22.770 --> 00:25:24.720
I want you to be happy, Bellana.

00:25:25.430 --> 00:25:26.110
Without you?

00:25:26.630 --> 00:25:26.750
What?

00:25:27.010 --> 00:25:27.270
Shh!

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:29.760
I'll always be.

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:32.310
I'm not fond of you. That will never change.

00:25:32.530 --> 00:25:36.660
You can't just leave me. I couldn't bear to be alone.

00:25:37.750 --> 00:25:40.800
Aren't you forgetting someone? He needs you, beloved.

00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:48.840
Forget him. He's not half the man you...

00:25:49.670 --> 00:25:50.590
Mm-hmm. No.

00:25:51.070 --> 00:25:52.150
I've seen enough of this.

00:25:54.080 --> 00:25:56.780
Alright, let's go back to sickbay and try to isolate that algorithm.

00:26:00.410 --> 00:26:01.070
Congratulations.

00:26:01.370 --> 00:26:02.970
Thank you for this opportunity, Captain.

00:26:04.440 --> 00:26:06.680
All I've ever wanted was to live up to my full potential,

00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:08.900
to hone all my skills,

00:26:09.950 --> 00:26:11.030
expand my abilities,

00:26:12.250 --> 00:26:13.450
to help the people I love.

00:26:22.060 --> 00:26:22.860
What's the status?

00:26:25.030 --> 00:26:26.430
I lost the signal again.

00:26:26.610 --> 00:26:27.810
I don't know what happened.

00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:29.980
Two assault vessels are...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:37.220
on course to join us accurate information is essential the more i learn about voyager the

00:26:37.220 --> 00:26:44.480
more i wonder if it's worth the trouble clarify launching an attack against such a heavily armed

00:26:44.480 --> 00:26:50.950
vessel carries a great risk and for what a little anti-matter and some dilithium your survey

00:26:50.950 --> 00:26:56.190
indicated large quantities of both we've already committed substantial resources to mounting this

00:26:56.190 --> 00:26:59.900
assault. Were you mistaken? No, not at all.

00:27:00.570 --> 00:27:03.710
I'm just sounding a note of caution.

00:27:05.080 --> 00:27:10.840
If our boarding party doesn't find Voyager exactly as you've described it,

00:27:12.210 --> 00:27:13.810
the hierarchy will be informed.

00:27:16.890 --> 00:27:20.160
I understand, but there has been no mistake.

00:27:24.060 --> 00:27:24.540
Proceed.

00:27:30.730 --> 00:27:39.130
made a terrible mistake. Oh, terrible. The doctor was appearing at a different location every few

00:27:39.130 --> 00:27:47.760
seconds. It didn't seem possible. So I investigated a little further and haven't been monitoring his

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:59.440
perceptions. I've been watching his dreams or his imaginings. I'm not sure which of this is real.

00:28:02.450 --> 00:28:29.720
I'm going to do came to check on your patient doing just fine captain took lieutenant Torres half the night to stabilize my matrix and had a single flight of fancy

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:35.880
I apologize for altering my program without permission.

00:28:36.110 --> 00:28:37.710
At least there wasn't any permanent debt.

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:40.620
I'm afraid there was.

00:28:42.840 --> 00:28:47.770
Exposed, humiliated, turned inside out for all the world to see.

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:50.520
I've lost your respect.

00:28:51.260 --> 00:28:52.100
That will never happen.

00:28:53.710 --> 00:28:56.370
Certainly not because we've seen a few random fantasies.

00:28:58.250 --> 00:28:59.450
We all daydreamed up.

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:02.940
It helps us imagine other possibilities in life.

00:29:04.120 --> 00:29:07.440
Just hold off until we've figured out a way for you to do it without damaging yourself.

00:29:07.920 --> 00:29:08.320
All right?

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:16.960
Come in.

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.140
Ship status report.

00:29:23.890 --> 00:29:24.670
Federation law.

00:29:25.860 --> 00:29:27.040
Thinking about a career change?

00:29:27.700 --> 00:29:28.200
In a way.

00:29:29.070 --> 00:29:29.850
Not for me, though.

00:29:31.370 --> 00:29:35.790
I've been going over the legal precedents for granting command positions to holograms.

00:29:36.420 --> 00:29:37.180
There aren't any.

00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:39.860
Captain, this ship needs its doctor.

00:29:40.040 --> 00:29:41.920
He should focus on what he was programmed for.

00:29:42.390 --> 00:29:43.150
Medical care.

00:29:43.720 --> 00:29:46.940
I think we've underestimated him because of our own human limitations.

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:49.920
His full potential's unknown, Chakotay.

00:29:50.460 --> 00:29:53.160
Would you be comfortable handing over your ship to a computer program?

00:29:53.610 --> 00:29:55.230
I don't know if I'd take it that far.

00:29:55.600 --> 00:29:56.360
You might have to.

00:29:57.450 --> 00:29:58.850
He probably won't settle for less.

00:30:18.590 --> 00:30:20.210
Allow me to shake your hand.

00:30:22.210 --> 00:30:22.590
Congratulations.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.800
Doctor, may I please have a word with you?

00:30:27.720 --> 00:30:29.060
I don't recall dreaming you up.

00:30:29.200 --> 00:30:29.680
You didn't.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.980
I'm transmitting a simulation of myself into your program, but I am real.

00:30:34.370 --> 00:30:37.450
Doctor to the bridge, I'm daydreaming again. Somebody deactivate me.

00:30:37.510 --> 00:30:38.910
Voyager is about to be attacked.

00:30:39.130 --> 00:30:42.170
Of course it is, unless the valiant doctor swings into action, right?

00:30:42.190 --> 00:30:43.290
Yes, yes, precisely.

00:30:43.490 --> 00:30:44.950
A common theme in all my fantasies.

00:30:45.070 --> 00:30:49.170
I reactivated your cognitive algorithms. I put you back into this fiction.

00:30:49.450 --> 00:30:56.570
It was the only way for me to communicate with you.

00:30:58.140 --> 00:30:59.490
Yes, that's right.

00:31:00.510 --> 00:31:07.860
I'm listening. I'm a long-range observer on an assault class vessel. I scan passing ships for

00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:12.540
Technology and raw materials when I find an acceptable target. We rate it

00:31:12.540 --> 00:31:17.200
You've been spying on us more to the point on you for several days

00:31:17.200 --> 00:31:20.820
I've been using a long-range tunneling sensor to tap into your program

00:31:20.820 --> 00:31:29.260
You were supposed to be our eyes and ears on Voyager instead. I got this daydreams

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:37.640
to my daydreams that's why my algorithms have been destabilizing my fault I'm sorry tell me

00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:43.020
about this attack my ship is less than an hour away I can help you avoid a confrontation but

00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:51.360
you must do exactly what I say why should you want to help us you don't understand the hierarchy does

00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:57.700
not tolerate mistakes or misinformation they learn of my error lose

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:08.660
my livelihood. Well, that's what you get for being a peeping Tom. But I also care about what

00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:16.270
happens to you. I feel like I've gotten to know you over the past few days. I've been spying on

00:32:16.270 --> 00:32:26.130
my fantasies, not me. You don't know me at all. But I do. I know how your mind works, what your

00:32:26.130 --> 00:32:29.730
hopes are. You created all these

00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:35.220
Possibilities. My species, we're very different.

00:32:35.770 --> 00:32:43.500
Our thinking is confined, but can't help but admire you.

00:32:46.110 --> 00:32:47.770
Don't want you to be harmed.

00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:54.910
We should swing into action.

00:32:58.560 --> 00:32:59.700
Captain, we're about to be attacked.

00:33:00.030 --> 00:33:01.290
Alien vessels are approaching.

00:33:02.440 --> 00:33:03.880
There's nothing on the sensors, Doc.

00:33:04.230 --> 00:33:05.430
The vessels are cloaked.

00:33:05.630 --> 00:33:06.290
How do you know this?

00:33:06.450 --> 00:33:07.730
One of the aliens contacted me.

00:33:07.970 --> 00:33:09.330
I've detected no transmissions.

00:33:09.490 --> 00:33:10.690
He spoke to me in a daydream.

00:33:10.810 --> 00:33:11.430
I don't want to hear it.

00:33:11.790 --> 00:33:14.390
However, I would like to know why you've disobeyed my direct order.

00:33:14.670 --> 00:33:15.670
I can prove it to you.

00:33:16.380 --> 00:33:20.320
The alien told me how to reconfigure our sensors to compensate for their cloaking field.

00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:28.420
He's right.

00:33:29.220 --> 00:33:29.980
I'm picking up...

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:34.590
Three ships out there. Distance, 600 million kilometers. Headed right for us.

00:33:35.060 --> 00:33:39.990
On screen. Maximum magnification.

00:33:53.700 --> 00:33:55.380
Won't help us unless we help him.

00:33:56.050 --> 00:33:58.500
What if this is all part of their attack? A ruse.

00:33:58.690 --> 00:33:59.830
He's already helped us compensate.

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:04.640
their cloak i'm inclined to believe in so am i but i just as soon set a course away from here at

00:34:04.640 --> 00:34:09.130
maximum warp that will only delay a confrontation they have vessels hidden throughout the entire

00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:14.800
sector did your friend have a plan he said they're running what's called a type 3 stealth assault

00:34:14.800 --> 00:34:18.420
they won't decloak until they're right on top of us at which point they'll fire a warning shot

00:34:18.420 --> 00:34:22.700
across our bow then come the demands for supplies and technology if we don't comply

00:34:22.700 --> 00:34:29.110
they'll destroy us fortunately the alien promised to transmit the resonance frequencies of their

00:34:29.110 --> 00:34:29.490
phasers.

00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:41.050
and in return return he mistakenly informed his appearance that i was in command voyager

00:34:41.050 --> 00:34:48.730
to keep himself from being demoted he wants us to maintain that fiction when they open the channel

00:34:48.730 --> 00:34:59.900
i have to be sitting in the captain's chair i'm sorry he insisted i guess it's time to turn

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:10.680
fantasy into reality i'm in over my head what if i fail you sound like i did when the captain put me

00:35:10.680 --> 00:35:15.700
in command of the night shift that chair looks so big i thought i'd sink so far into it that nobody

00:35:15.700 --> 00:35:20.220
would be able to see me but you had your academy training to fall back on yeah well sounds like

00:35:20.220 --> 00:35:25.830
you've had plenty of practice that wasn't real listen doc the whole reason you wanted to be able

00:35:25.830 --> 00:35:28.550
to daydream was to test out possibilities right

00:35:31.470 --> 00:35:32.450
Consider this a field test.

00:35:32.610 --> 00:35:38.470
Why isn't there any hull damage from the Borg attack?

00:35:38.930 --> 00:35:41.650
They repaired it so quickly.

00:35:42.660 --> 00:35:47.060
Prepare for Type 4 assault.

00:35:47.720 --> 00:35:51.640
Type 4? That would cause a huge drain on our energy core.

00:35:51.920 --> 00:35:53.840
A waste of resources.

00:35:54.710 --> 00:35:56.430
Do you really think that's necessary?

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:57.820
What I think doesn't matter.

00:35:58.680 --> 00:35:59.960
Your long-range surveillance...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:06.170
indicated an attack by Borg. On closer inspection, that appears to be doubtful. Your report on this

00:36:06.170 --> 00:36:25.830
vessel could be mistaken. I think caution is in order. He agrees. Proceed to type four.

00:36:36.780 --> 00:36:37.440
Captain on the bridge.

00:36:56.440 --> 00:36:59.980
But what I wouldn't give right now for a...

00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:00.870
A whoopee cushion.

00:37:01.660 --> 00:37:02.100
A what?

00:37:04.060 --> 00:37:04.960
Ancient technology.

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:31.400
Captain, we're ready to proceed.

00:37:32.630 --> 00:37:33.390
Acknowledged, Commander.

00:37:34.210 --> 00:37:35.550
The internal comm link is active.

00:37:36.330 --> 00:37:37.850
No one will be able to hear you but the Doctor.

00:37:38.760 --> 00:37:39.620
Doctor, are you ready?

00:37:41.250 --> 00:37:43.060
No, but do I have a choice?

00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:45.100
Every step of the way.

00:37:48.520 --> 00:37:48.860
Understood.

00:37:49.860 --> 00:37:51.940
I'm receiving a transmission on a secure channel.

00:37:52.410 --> 00:37:53.070
Audio only.

00:37:53.540 --> 00:37:54.620
Must be the Doctor's friend.

00:37:54.920 --> 00:37:57.450
Let's hear what he has to say, Doctor.

00:37:59.090 --> 00:37:59.290
Hello?

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:02.920
Voyager here. It's me.

00:38:04.910 --> 00:38:09.510
Something terrible has happened. Ordered a Type 4 Assault.

00:38:09.920 --> 00:38:15.500
Our phaser frequencies will be rotated continuously. Be able to help you.

00:38:16.140 --> 00:38:19.360
Evasive maneuvers. Three vessels are decloaking off the port bow.

00:38:20.150 --> 00:38:24.830
That didn't feel like a warning shot.

00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:27.020
Direct hit. Shields are holding.

00:38:27.910 --> 00:38:28.550
They're hailing us.

00:38:30.410 --> 00:38:32.740
This is it, Doctor. On screen.

00:38:35.760 --> 00:38:36.460
There he is.

00:38:38.730 --> 00:38:41.100
Careful, he's dangerous.

00:38:41.460 --> 00:38:46.680
The hierarchy controls this region of space.

00:38:47.090 --> 00:38:49.910
Your ship has supplies and technology that we require.

00:38:50.640 --> 00:38:52.160
Tell him we'll defend ourselves.

00:38:52.480 --> 00:38:54.180
They won't get what they're after.

00:38:55.170 --> 00:38:57.860
We'll defend ourselves. They won't get what they're after.

00:38:58.630 --> 00:38:58.830
Huh?

00:38:58.990 --> 00:38:59.800
I mean you.

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:05.440
Won't get what you're after. Not in a million years. Not if I have anything to say about it.

00:39:05.790 --> 00:39:07.030
Don't improvise, Doctor.

00:39:07.750 --> 00:39:08.050
Sorry.

00:39:08.970 --> 00:39:13.450
An exchange of fire would damage both of our ships.

00:39:14.050 --> 00:39:16.660
But we have support nearby. You are alone.

00:39:17.260 --> 00:39:19.740
Take your weapons offline and prepare to be...

00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:22.020
Excuse the interruption, Commander.

00:39:22.420 --> 00:39:24.580
I've found a potential weakness in their shields.

00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:27.280
But I'll need time to reconfigure our phasers.

00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:29.300
Keep him occupied, Doctor.

00:39:30.250 --> 00:39:30.730
On screen.

00:39:31.210 --> 00:39:33.690
This is my final warning.

00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:35.540
Don't rush me.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:37.320
Take your weapons offline.

00:39:37.520 --> 00:39:38.060
Immediately.

00:39:38.200 --> 00:39:39.740
I won't ask again.

00:39:39.880 --> 00:39:44.730
You appear to be suffering from a physio-emotive disorder.

00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:47.920
You're impatient, quick to anger.

00:39:48.280 --> 00:39:50.810
Do you have any idea what that does to your vascular pressure?

00:39:51.010 --> 00:39:52.250
You may want to see a physician.

00:39:52.510 --> 00:39:53.490
Firing phasers.

00:39:57.710 --> 00:39:58.170
Correct hit.

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:02.440
How do you like that, huh? A taste of your own medicine!

00:40:02.690 --> 00:40:04.090
Tone it down, doctor.

00:40:04.510 --> 00:40:04.750
Sorry.

00:40:11.720 --> 00:40:12.600
Phasers are offline.

00:40:13.350 --> 00:40:14.690
Prepare to be boarded.

00:40:17.710 --> 00:40:18.190
Tuba!

00:40:25.620 --> 00:40:27.880
Evade the photonic cannon.

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:33.700
That was an order!

00:40:38.370 --> 00:40:41.170
Activating the photonic cannon, sir.

00:40:42.840 --> 00:40:45.340
I'd rather not give the order to fire.

00:40:47.150 --> 00:40:49.450
My sensors are showing no activation sequence.

00:40:49.750 --> 00:40:53.060
Of course not. The photonic cannon is impervious to sensors.

00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:56.960
Couldn't detect it either. That's why they were destroyed.

00:40:58.230 --> 00:40:59.250
Borg the hierarchy.

00:41:00.160 --> 00:41:04.910
The same to me. Just another bully who didn't know when to back off.

00:41:05.490 --> 00:41:07.130
We'll be vaporized.

00:41:24.100 --> 00:41:24.920
Suggest retreat.

00:41:32.110 --> 00:41:33.550
Moving away at maximum impulse.

00:41:43.440 --> 00:41:45.720
Doctor, you burned it.

00:42:00.540 --> 00:42:01.640
Seven of nine to the doctor.

00:42:02.250 --> 00:42:02.590
Go ahead.

00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:05.100
I require your assistance in the mess hall.

00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:08.270
I'll be right there.

00:42:18.270 --> 00:42:18.790
Hurry, doc.

00:42:19.070 --> 00:42:19.670
You're not dreaming.

00:42:20.460 --> 00:42:20.760
Captain.

00:42:24.100 --> 00:42:29.970
For your imaginative defense of this ship and her crew, I'm awarding you the Starfleet

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:35.680
Medal of Commendation. Congratulations. Thank you. I've also reconsidered your

00:42:35.680 --> 00:42:39.640
request. I'm going to authorize a research project to explore your

00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:52.250
command abilities. You're a natural. Congratulations. It was a platonic

00:42:52.250 --> 00:42:55.600
gesture. Don't expect me to pose for you. Noted.
